{
  "contract": {
    "id": "mailbox-adapters",
    "version": 1
  },
  "description": "The CLI versions each mailbox hook adapter is proven against (docs/platform/agent-mailbox/spec.md §4.1, spelled testedAgainst here), and the measured hook facts of each drained CLI (hookFacts). A version is listed only when its Stop and PostToolUse payloads and the output shapes the CLI injected were recorded on it; the fixtures live under fixtures/hooks/<cli>/. hookFacts are per CLI, not per version: hookTopology (direct: the CLI starts the hook itself, or its in-process extension does (pi, omp); one-shell-hop: through one shell that does not exec it), hookShell (the path the CLI invokes for the hook command, checked against the hop parent's executable and argv[0]; null for direct), headExecutables (exe basenames accepted at the direct head position), headComm (optional: the command name a direct head must also carry where its executable is not specific to the CLI, pi on node), postToolUseContextMaxBytes (the bound of a PostToolUse drain's output; null means no PostToolUse drain) and channels: for stop and postToolUse, whether that hook delivers mail (deliver), the role its injected text reaches the model under (role) and where that role was recorded (source). A provider-level message role is written as it is (user, developer); a role prefixed transcript: is the CLI's transcript record type, recorded where the provider-level role was not. No delivering channel may have role user: a user-role channel turns a peer's mail into the user's own request. A postToolUse channel delivers exactly when postToolUseContextMaxBytes is set. measuredOn names the versions the facts were measured on, and for a CLI that routes to several providers the provider converter the channel roles were recorded through (provider); re-recording a new version re-measures them. A CLI of the first slice that could not be proven is listed under deferred with its reason, never left out silently.",
  "source": "hookFacts: plans/reports/research-261023-0148-mailbox-v5-measurements.md tables (b), (c), (d), (e), (f) and (g); the bound applies plan decision 6's margin rule for a threshold shown to apply per hook (the largest inline ladder step, 9,216 bytes, less one ladder step of 1,024 bytes), in both CLIs",
  "testedAgainst": [
